# Mahal — Feature Scope, User Roles & Admin Requirements

**Status:** Draft for review
**Scope:** Defines who uses Mahal, what each role can do, what ships in v1 vs later, and what platform operators need to run it.
**Grounding assumption:** The core transaction primitive is **RFQ → Proposal → Booking**, not ticket sales. Every role and feature below is built around that loop, plus the three adjacent layers (contributor directory, venue booking, sponsorship).

---

## 1. Identity Model — Accounts vs. Roles

Before listing roles, one structural decision drives everything else: **a person/company is one Identity that can hold multiple Role Profiles.**

A single user account (one login, one Identity record) can attach one or more of: Client Profile, Provider Profile, Venue Profile, Sponsor Profile. This matters in this market specifically because it's common for the same company to be, e.g., an event agency (Provider) that also books venues (Client) and occasionally sponsors industry events (Sponsor). Forcing separate logins per role would fragment reputation, billing, and messaging history that should stay unified.

This keeps Identity/Access (schema group 1) clean and generic, while each role's specifics live in its own profile table (schema group 3) — consistent with the direction already set.

---

## 2. User Roles

| Role | Who they are | Core capability |
|---|---|---|
| **Client / Organizer** | Anyone posting event work — corporates, agencies, individuals planning weddings/events | Posts RFQs, reviews proposals, books providers & venues, pays, rates |
| **Provider — Freelancer** | Individual service seller (photographer, MC, decorator, etc.) | Browses/matches to RFQs, submits proposals, fulfills bookings |
| **Provider — Vendor/Agency** | Company-level service seller with a team | Same as freelancer, plus manages sub-users/team members under one profile |
| **Venue Owner/Manager** | Lists physical space(s) for events | Manages listing(s), availability, pricing, responds to venue RFQs/bookings |
| **Contributor** *(tier, not a separate account type — see below)* | Any Provider or Venue opting into paid directory placement | Enhanced visibility, badge, featured placement — governed by subscription tier |
| **Sponsor / Brand Partner** | Brands seeking event association/placement | Browses sponsorship opportunities, submits offers, manages sponsorship deals |
| **Platform Admin** | Internal Mahal staff | Full platform oversight — see Section 4 |
| **Support/Trust & Safety Agent** | Internal staff, scoped admin | Verification review, dispute handling, content moderation — subset of Admin permissions |

**Open question to confirm:** does a Venue need its own role distinct from Provider, or is "Venue" simply a Provider whose category is "Venue Rental"? I've treated it as structurally distinct here (separate profile shape — capacity, floor plans, amenities — vs. a service provider's portfolio/skills shape), because the two have almost no overlapping fields. But if you want venues folded into the general Provider taxonomy to simplify the schema, that's a valid alternative — it changes schema group 3 from 2 profile shapes to 1 with conditional fields.

